# Single source of truth (Scott Ops Platform)

Full detail: `docs/laws.md` and `docs/ONE_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH_ROADMAP.md`. Apply to every
migration and module in this build. These rules do NOT license refactoring the Scott
API section (see freeze below).

## Nine laws (enforce in the database)

1. One master per entity; transactions reference master IDs — never free-text party/SKU names.
2. Stock is an append-only ledger with reason + reference document; on-hand is a sum, never edited.
3. Money is a document (invoice, credit/debit note, receipt, bill) — never a cell.
4. Every document has a DB-enforced state machine + an audit row (who/when/from/to).
5. One owner per location; cross-boundary moves are explicit transfer documents.
6. After cutover, sheets export from the platform, never into it.
7. Tally is the statutory ledger; post vouchers, reconcile daily.
8. Every report is a SQL view; one metric definition, in a metric dictionary, with an owner.
9. Access is enforced by RLS, not the UI; verify with direct API calls.

## Six-question gate (before building any module)

Which master? Are quantities movements? Is money a document? What state machine?
Which view reports it? Which role sees it? Can't answer all six → not ready.

## Correctness (non-negotiable)

- Stock/money mutations live in DB functions with `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` + tests; never in client code.
- Documents immutable once numbered/posted; correct with reversing documents + reason.
- Sequences gapless per entity × GSTIN × doc type × FY.
- Never hard-delete; status `cancelled`. `entity_id` + `gstin_id` on every document.
- Staging first (`scvojtvgnkmbupvyslmb`); production only on explicit release.
- Table prefixes: `core_ cat_ crm_ inv_ po_ so_ jw_ bill_ ar_ ap_ uni_ dist_ cost_ prod_ hr_ rpt_`.

## FROZEN — do not touch the Scott API section

Never modify/rename/re-prefix: `src/scott/**`, sidebar tabs `scott_customers` /
`scott_reports` / `scott_masters` (group "Scott API"), `scott-*` edge functions
(incl. `scott-dashboard-masters`), `docs/SCOTT_API.md`, `docs/SCOTT_INTEGRATION_REFERENCE.md`,
and the existing inventory-fetch integration tables (mirror source — read-only for new modules).
New masters inherit existing SKU codes exactly; nothing the integration maps on is renamed.
